title: A call waiting on the old child during a shutdown spawns a child after the
  shutdown
updated: 2026-11-10T16:02:49Z
---

Found by mcp-hub-worker during wave C (k185/k191/k187, 2026-11-10). A call that waits on _gone_p while the daemon shuts down goes on to start_p once the old child is gone; the hub still holds the upstream, so k191's let-go guard does not apply, and shutdown_p has already resolved -- a child is spawned after the shutdown. Fix: start_p refuses while the hub is shutting down. Test in t/shutdown.t.
